## Course Overview

This course covers the dynamic modeling, analysis, and feedback control system design principles for industrial processes. Students gain practical insights into controller tuning and stability criteria for single-input single-output (SISO) control loops.

- Understand end-to-end process dynamics and transfer function derivation
- Analyze transient and steady-state responses of first and second-order systems
- Design and tune PID controllers using classical methods
- Implement feedforward, cascade, and ratio control strategies

## Prerequisites

- Differential Equations
- Basics of Linear Systems Theory

## Textbooks & References

- "Process Dynamics and Control" by Dale E. Seborg, Thomas F. Edgar, Duncan A. Mellichamp, Francis J. Doyle III
- "Feedback Control of Dynamic Systems" by Gene F. Franklin, J. David Powell, Abbas Emami-Naeini

